Governor [[Sarah Huckabee Sanders]], a Republican, was elected in [[2022 Arkansas gubernatorial election|2022]] with 63.1% of the vote. She is seeking re-election to a second term and ran unopposed for the Republican nomination.<ref name="SHS2026">{{cite news |last1=Barrow |first1=Bill |title=Project 2028: GOP officials jockey during Republican National Convention for future White House runs |url=https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-future-republican-candidates-253224301e5730b4309f97b1971b2fb4 |access-date=August 3, 2024 |publisher=[[Associated Press]] |date=July 18, 2024 |quote=[Sarah Huckabee Sanders] was focused only on Trump's election and then her own reelection in 2026 |archive-date=August 3, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240803045038/https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-future-republican-candidates-253224301e5730b4309f97b1971b2fb4 |url-status=live }}</ref>

[[Arkansas Senate|State senator]] [[Fredrick Love]]<ref name="LoveAR">{{cite news |last1=Brock |first1=Roby |title=Democratic State Sen. Fred Love announces for Arkansas Governor |url=https://talkbusiness.net/2025/06/democratic-state-sen-fred-love-announces-for-arkansas-governor/ |access-date=June 23, 2025 |work=Talk Business & Politics |date=June 23, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250623151433/https://talkbusiness.net/2025/06/democratic-state-sen-fred-love-announces-for-arkansas-governor/ |archive-date=June 23, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> defeated former [[Walmart]] executive Supha Xayprasith Mays<ref>{{cite web |last1=Wickline |first1=Michael R. |title=Bentonville businesswoman running again for governor |url=https://www.nwaonline.com/news/2025/oct/28/bentonville-businesswoman-running-again-for/ |access-date=November 3, 2025 |work=[[Northwest Arkansas Democrat-Gazette]] |date=October 28, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260218032545/https://www.nwaonline.com/news/2025/oct/28/bentonville-businesswoman-running-again-for/ |archive-date=February 18, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> in the Democratic primary on March 3, 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Arkansas Election Night Reporting |url=https://enr.totalresults.com/arkansas#election=7f77a178-af02-40ec-92db-c5cc50882c68&contest=32eedf4d-f628-4868-8ddc-10b83bdd8030&filter=Statewide&bucket=results |access-date=2026-03-26 |website=enr.totalresults.com |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260322053722/https://enr.totalresults.com/arkansas#election=7f77a178-af02-40ec-92db-c5cc50882c68&contest=32eedf4d-f628-4868-8ddc-10b83bdd8030&filter=Statewide&bucket=results |archive-date=March 22, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

[[Farmer]] Colt Shelby is running in the general election as a [[Libertarian Party (United States)|Libertarian]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Brock |first=Roby |date=2026-02-23 |title=Arkansas Libertarians nominate candidates for 2026 |url=https://talkbusiness.net/2026/02/arkansas-libertarians-nominate-candidates-for-2026/ |access-date=2026-03-26 |website=Talk Business & Politics |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260304184917/https://talkbusiness.net/2026/02/arkansas-libertarians-nominate-candidates-for-2026/ |archive-date=March 4, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Sarah Huckabee Sanders was re-elected.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Grajeda |first=Antoinette |date=2026-11-04 |title=Sarah Huckabee Sanders wins second term as Arkansas governor |url=https://arkansasadvocate.com/2026/11/03/sarah-huckabee-sanders-wins-second-term-as-arkansas-governor/ |access-date=2026-11-14 |website=Arkansas Advocate |language=en-US}}</ref> Shelby became the first third-party Arkansas gubernatorial candidate to win a county since [[1896 Arkansas gubernatorial election|1896]] when he carried his home county of [[Franklin County, Arkansas|Franklin]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Colt Shelby wins county as third party candidate in Arkansas for first time since 1800s|url=https://www.5newsonline.com/video/news/politics/elections/colt-shelby-wins-county-as-third-party-candidate-in-arkansas-for-first-time-since-1800s/527-0d29a6e8-bb3b-45a8-a893-532ca6d318fc|access-date=4 November 2026|work=5newsonline.com|date=4 November 2026}}</ref>
