Governor [[Jared Polis]], a Democrat, was re-elected in [[2022 Colorado gubernatorial election|2022]] with 58.5% of the vote. He will be term-limited by the [[Colorado Constitution]] in 2026 and cannot seek re-election to a third consecutive term.

[[Attorney General of Colorado|State Attorney General]] [[Phil Weiser]]<ref name=Weiser>{{cite news |last=Paul |first=Jesse |access-date=January 2, 2025 |title=Colorado Attorney General Phil Weiser launches 2026 campaign for governor |date=January 2, 2025 |url=https://coloradosun.com/2025/01/02/phil-weiser-colorado-governor-2026/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250102184008/https://coloradosun.com/2025/01/02/phil-weiser-colorado-governor-2026/ |archive-date=January 2, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> defeated [[United States Senate|U.S. Senator]] [[Michael Bennet]]<ref name="Bennet Announcement">{{cite web |last1=Kim |first1=Caitlyn |title=Sen. Michael Bennet is officially running for governor |url=https://www.cpr.org/2025/04/11/michael-bennet-running-for-colorado-governor/ |website=[[Colorado Public Radio]] |access-date=April 11, 2025 |date=April 11, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250411130600/https://www.cpr.org/2025/04/11/michael-bennet-running-for-colorado-governor/ |archive-date=April 11, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> for the Democratic nomination.

On the Republican side, ministry leader [[Victor Marx]] defeated state representative [[Scott Bottoms]] and state senator [[Barbara Kirkmeyer]] for the nomination.<ref name="BottomsCO">{{Cite web |last=Paul |first=Jesse |access-date=January 21, 2025 |title=Scott Bottoms, Republican state representative, will run for Colorado governor in 2026 |date=January 20, 2025 |url=https://coloradosun.com/2025/01/20/scott-bottoms-colorado-governor-2026/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250120183306/https://coloradosun.com/2025/01/20/scott-bottoms-colorado-governor-2026/ |archive-date=January 20, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="KirkmeyerCO">{{cite news |last1=Paul |first1=Jesse |title=Republican Barbara Kirkmeyer is running to be Colorado's next governor |url=https://coloradosun.com/2025/09/09/barbara-kirkmeyer-colorado-governor-2026/ |access-date=September 9, 2025 |work=The Colorado Sun |date=September 9, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250909173110/https://coloradosun.com/2025/09/09/barbara-kirkmeyer-colorado-governor-2026/ |archive-date=September 9, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Former [[U.S. Representative]] for Colorado's 4th congressional district [[Greg Lopez]] initially announced his campaign as a Republican but later left the party in January 2026 and is continuing his campaign as an independent.<ref name="LopezCO">{{cite news |last1=Metzger |first1=Hannah |title=Lopez launches third Republican run for Colorado governor |url=https://www.9news.com/article/news/local/local-politics/greg-lopez-colorado-governor-candidate-republican/73-74af91fa-7429-451d-bdad-88d5c509c3b9 |access-date=April 14, 2025 |work=9News |date=April 14, 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref name="LopezInd">{{cite news |last1=Paul |first1=Jesse |title=Major shake-up in crowded Republican primary for Colorado governor as one candidate leaves race, another leaves GOP |url=https://coloradosun.com/2026/01/05/mark-baisley-greg-lopez-colorado-governors-race/ |access-date=January 7, 2026 |work=The Colorado Sun |date=January 5, 2026 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260107013435/https://coloradosun.com/2026/01/05/mark-baisley-greg-lopez-colorado-governors-race/ |archive-date=January 7, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Weiser defeated Marx and Lopez in a landslide.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Paul |first=Jesse |date=2026-11-04 |title=Democrat Phil Weiser easily beats Republican Victor Marx to become Colorado's next governor |url=https://coloradosun.com/2026/11/03/colorado-governor-election-results/ |access-date=2026-11-14 |website=The Colorado Sun |language=en-US}}</ref>
