[[List of governors of Connecticut|Governor]] [[Ned Lamont]], a Democrat, was re-elected in [[2022 Connecticut gubernatorial election|2022]] with 56% of the vote. Because [[Connecticut]] does not have gubernatorial term limits in its [[Constitution of Connecticut|Constitution]], Lamont has announced that he is running for a third term.<ref name=Lamont>{{cite news|last=Cerulli|first=Mike|access-date=November 7, 2025|title=Ned Lamont to run for third term as Connecticut governor in 2026: Sources|date=November 7, 2025|url=https://www.wtnh.com/news/elections/ned-lamont-to-run-for-third-term-as-connecticut-governor-in-2026-sources/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251107230446/https://www.wtnh.com/news/elections/ned-lamont-to-run-for-third-term-as-connecticut-governor-in-2026-sources/|archive-date=November 7, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> Lamont fended off a primary challenge from [[Connecticut House of Representatives|State representative]] for the 88th district [[Josh Elliott (politician)|Josh Elliott]].<ref name=Pazniokas>{{cite news |last=Pazniokas |first=Mark |access-date=July 11, 2025 |title=Rep. Josh Elliott files to challenge Lamont for governor |date=July 8, 2025 |url=https://ctmirror.org/2025/07/08/rep-josh-elliott-files-to-challenge-lamont-for-governor/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250710161057/https://ctmirror.org/2025/07/08/rep-josh-elliott-files-to-challenge-lamont-for-governor/ |archive-date=July 10, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

[[Connecticut State Senate|State senator]] for the 36th district [[Ryan Fazio]] is the Republican nominee.<ref name="Fazio">{{cite news |title=Sen. Ryan Fazio announces run for governor in 2026 |url=https://www.nbcconnecticut.com/news/politics/sen-ryan-fazio-announces-run-for-governor-in-2026/3624953/ |access-date=August 13, 2025 |work=NBC Connecticut |date=August 13, 2025}}</ref> Former [[lieutenant governor of New York]] [[Betsy McCaughey]]<ref>{{Cite web |author=Luke Parsnow |title=Former New York lieutenant governor announces run for governor of Connecticut |url=https://spectrumlocalnews.com/nys/central-ny/politics/2026/01/15/betsy-mccaughey-announces-run-for-governor-in-connecticut |access-date=2026-03-26 |website=spectrumlocalnews.com |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260518164315/https://spectrumlocalnews.com/nys/central-ny/politics/2026/01/15/betsy-mccaughey-announces-run-for-governor-in-connecticut |archive-date=May 18, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> initially announced her candidacy for the Republican nomination in March 2026 but withdrew after not receiving 15% of the convention vote in May. New Britain mayor [[Erin Stewart]] initially ran but dropped out of the race in May 2026, after allegations of misconduct during her tenure as mayor.<ref name="StewartCT">{{cite news |last1=Pazniokas |first1=Mark |title=Erin Stewart kicks off campaign for CT governor |url=https://ctmirror.org/2025/11/18/erin-stewart-kicks-off-campaign-for-ct-governor/ |access-date=November 18, 2025 |work=[[The Connecticut Mirror]] |date=November 18, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251118152233/https://ctmirror.org/2025/11/18/erin-stewart-kicks-off-campaign-for-ct-governor/ |archive-date=November 18, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Republican Erin Stewart suspends campaign for Connecticut governor amid report of misconduct|url=https://www.ctinsider.com/politics/article/erin-stewart-suspends-campaign-governor-fazio-22258746.php|date=May 14, 2026|author=Putterman, Alex|website=CT Insider|access-date=May 14, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260514192323/https://www.ctinsider.com/politics/article/erin-stewart-suspends-campaign-governor-fazio-22258746.php|archive-date=May 14, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref>

Lamont defeated Fazio by nearly 20 points.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Glatz |first=Jennifer |date=2026-11-03 |title=Gov. Ned Lamont wins third term as Connecticut's governor. See how your town voted |url=https://www.nbcconnecticut.com/elections/connecticut-governor-election-results-lamont-fazio-midterms/3787870/ |access-date=2026-11-14 |website=NBC Connecticut |language=en-US}}</ref>
