{{See also|2026 Idaho lieutenant gubernatorial election}}
[[Governor of Idaho|Governor]] [[Brad Little]], a Republican, was re-elected in [[2022 Idaho gubernatorial election|2022]] with 60.5% of the vote. Because [[Idaho]] does not have gubernatorial term limits in its [[Constitution of Idaho|Constitution]], he is running for re-election to a third term.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-02-24 |title=Idaho Governor Brad Little announces bid for a third term as state leader |url=https://www.ktvb.com/article/news/local/idaho-governor-announces-bid-for-a-third-term-as-state-leader/277-0d9022d1-8685-4827-a78c-2c62e6d8a40e |access-date=2026-03-26 |website=ktvb.com |language=en-US}}</ref>

Attorney Terri Pickens, who was the Democratic nominee for [[Lieutenant Governor of Idaho|lieutenant governor]] in [[2022 Idaho lieutenant gubernatorial election|2022]], is running for the Democratic gubernatorial nomination.<ref name="Pickens">{{cite news |title=Boise lawyer announces Democratic run for Idaho governor |url=https://www.kmvt.com/2025/11/11/boise-lawyer-announces-democratic-run-idaho-governor/ |access-date=November 28, 2025 |work=[[KMVT]] |date=November 11, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251111232055/https://www.kmvt.com/2025/11/11/boise-lawyer-announces-democratic-run-idaho-governor/ |archive-date=November 11, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Former Republican [[John Stegner]], a former justice of the [[Idaho Supreme Court]], announced an independent campaign.<ref name="Stegner">{{Cite web |title=Former Idaho Supreme Court Justice eyes governorship|url=https://cdapress.com/news/2026/feb/06/former-idaho-supreme-court-justice-eyes-governorship-in-independent-bid/|access-date=February 6, 2026|website=cdapress|date=February 6, 2026}}</ref><ref name="filing">{{cite web |title=Idaho Candidate Filing Portal - ReFrame|url=https://run.voteidaho.gov/search|website=Vote Idaho|access-date=24 February 2026}}</ref>

Little won re-election by a nearly 25-point margin.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-11-04 |title=Brad Little wins Governor of Idaho |url=https://www.kmvt.com/2026/11/04/brad-little-wins-governor-idaho/ |access-date=2026-11-14 |website=www.kmvt.com |language=en}}</ref>
