Governor [[Maura Healey]], a Democrat, was elected in [[2022 Massachusetts gubernatorial election|2022]] with 63.7% of the vote. Healey is running for re-election for a second term in office.<ref name="MauraHealey">{{cite news |last1=Van Buskirk |first1=Chris |title=Massachusetts Gov. Maura Healey says she plans to run for reelection in 2026 |url=https://www.bostonherald.com/2025/02/07/massachusetts-gov-maura-healey-says-she-plans-to-run-for-reelection-in-2026/ |access-date=February 7, 2025 |work=[[Boston Herald]] |date=February 7, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250208040532/https://www.bostonherald.com/2025/02/07/massachusetts-gov-maura-healey-says-she-plans-to-run-for-reelection-in-2026/ |archive-date=February 8, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

On the Republican side, businessman Mike Minogue defeated former chief administrator and acting general manager of the [[Massachusetts Bay Transportation Authority]] Brian Shortsleeve<ref name="Shortsleeve">{{cite news |last1=Van Buskirk |first1=Chris |title=Former MBTA chief administrator Brian Shortsleeve launches Republican run for governor |url=https://www.bostonherald.com/2025/05/12/former-mbta-chief-administrator-brian-shortsleeve-launches-republican-run-for-governor/ |access-date=May 12, 2025 |work=[[Boston Herald]] |date=May 12, 2025}}</ref> on September 1, 2026.<ref name="Minogue">{{cite web |last1=Whooley |first1=Sean |title=Former Abiomed CEO to run for Governor of Massachusetts |url=https://www.massdevice.com/former-abiomed-ceo-run-governor-massachusetts/ |access-date=October 1, 2025 |website=MassDevice |date=October 1, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251001195028/https://www.massdevice.com/former-abiomed-ceo-run-governor-massachusetts/ |archive-date=October 1, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Healey defeated Minogue by over 27 points.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Dumcius |first=Gintautas |date=2026-11-03 |title=Healey wins second term, defeating GOP challenger Mike Minogue |url=https://www.wbur.org/news/2026/11/03/massachusetts-healey-governor-race-election-result |access-date=2026-11-14 |website=www.wbur.org |language=en}}</ref>
