{{main|2026 Nebraska gubernatorial election}}

Governor [[Jim Pillen]], a Republican, was elected in [[2022 Nebraska gubernatorial election|2022]] with 59.7% of the vote. He is running for re-election to a second term.<ref name="PillenNE">{{cite news |last1=Anderson |first1=Jake |title='Make our great state even greater': Jim Pillen announces reelection bid as Nebraska's governor |url=https://www.ketv.com/article/nebraska-jim-pillen-running-reelection-governor/64916825 |access-date=May 29, 2025 |work=[[KETV]] |date=May 29, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250529155334/https://www.ketv.com/article/nebraska-jim-pillen-running-reelection-governor/64916825 |archive-date=May 29, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He faced some challenges in the Republican primary, including medicinal cannabis activist Jacy Todd.<ref name="JacyTodd">{{cite news |last1=Wendling |first1=Zach |title=Medical cannabis advocate, targeted notary running for Nebraska governor |url=https://nebraskaexaminer.com/2025/07/08/medical-cannabis-advocate-targeted-notary-running-for-nebraska-governor/ |access-date=July 8, 2025 |work=Nebraska Examiner |date=July 8, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250708121323/https://nebraskaexaminer.com/2025/07/08/medical-cannabis-advocate-targeted-notary-running-for-nebraska-governor/ |archive-date=July 8, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Former [[Nebraska Legislature|state senator]] and [[2018 Nebraska gubernatorial election|2018]] Democratic nominee for lieutenant governor [[Lynne Walz]] is the Democratic nominee.<ref name="WalzNE">{{cite news |last1=Anderson |first1=Jake |title=Former Nebraska state senator Lynne Walz announces campaign for governor |url=https://www.ketv.com/article/nebraska-governor-2026-election-state-senator-campaign/69514033 |access-date=November 24, 2025 |work=[[KETV]] |date=November 24, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251124140703/https://www.ketv.com/article/nebraska-governor-2026-election-state-senator-campaign/69514033 |archive-date=November 24, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Pillen won re-election over Walz by eight points,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wendling |first=Zach |date=2026-11-04 |title=Nebraska Gov. Jim Pillen wins reelection • Nebraska Examiner |url=https://nebraskaexaminer.com/2026/11/04/nebraska-gov-jim-pillen-wins-reelection/ |access-date=2026-11-14 |website=Nebraska Examiner |language=en-US}}</ref> the best performance for a Democrat in a Nebraska gubernatorial election since [[1994 Nebraska gubernatorial election|1994]], which was also the most recent time that Democrats won a gubernatorial election in Nebraska. This was also the closest gubernatorial election in Nebraska since [[1990 Nebraska gubernatorial election|1990]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Wendling|first1=Zach|title=Election 2026 by the numbers in Nebraska: a 93-county breakdown • Nebraska Examiner|url=https://nebraskaexaminer.com/2026/11/10/election-2026-by-the-numbers-in-nebraska-a-93-county-breakdown/|website=Nebraska Examiner|access-date=10 November 2026|date=10 November 2026}}</ref>
