{{See also|2026 Nevada lieutenant gubernatorial election}}
Governor [[Joe Lombardo]], a Republican, was elected in [[2022 Nevada gubernatorial election|2022]] with 48.8% of the vote and is running for re-election to a second term in office.<ref name=Lombardo>{{cite news |title=Nevada Gov. Joe Lombardo launches re-election campaign |first1=Kyle |last1=Chouinard |work=[[Las Vegas Sun]] |date=September 15, 2025 |access-date=September 16, 2025 |url=https://lasvegassun.com/news/2025/sep/15/nevada-gov-joe-lombardo-launches-re-election-campa/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250916063811/https://lasvegassun.com/news/2025/sep/15/nevada-gov-joe-lombardo-launches-re-election-campa/ |archive-date=September 16, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Businesswoman Irina Hansen, who ran for [[Mayor of Las Vegas]] in [[2024 Las Vegas mayoral election|2024]], challenged Lombardo in the GOP primary.<ref name="HansenNV">{{cite news |title=Irina Hansen announces candidacy for Nevada governor in 2026 race |url=https://news3lv.com/news/local/irina-hansen-announces-candidacy-for-nevada-governor-in-2026-race |access-date=June 18, 2025 |work=KSNV |date=June 18, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251008033155/https://news3lv.com/news/local/irina-hansen-announces-candidacy-for-nevada-governor-in-2026-race |archive-date=October 8, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Lombardo easily defeated Hansen with over 90% of the vote on June 9 and became the Republican nominee.

[[Nevada Attorney General|State attorney general]] [[Aaron Ford]] defeated [[Washoe County, Nevada|Washoe County]] Commissioner [[Alexis Hill (Nevada politician)|Alexis Hill]] for the Democratic nomination.<ref name="FordNV">{{cite news |last1=Seeman |first1=Matthew |title=Nevada Attorney General Aaron Ford formally launches campaign for governor |url=https://news3lv.com/news/local/nevada-attorney-general-aaron-ford-formally-launches-campaign-governor-gubernatorial-democratic-party-politics-joe-lombardo-republican-las-vegas-reno-carson-city |access-date=July 28, 2025 |work=[[KSNV]] |date=July 28, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260814042200/https://news3lv.com/news/local/nevada-attorney-general-aaron-ford-formally-launches-campaign-governor-gubernatorial-democratic-party-politics-joe-lombardo-republican-las-vegas-reno-carson-city |archive-date=August 14, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://thenevadaindependent.com/article/democrat-alexis-hill-jumps-into-nevada-governor-race-unveils-revenue-raising-tax-plan|title=Democrat Alexis Hill jumps into Nevada governor race, unveils revenue-raising tax plan|date=September 4, 2025|website=The Nevada Independent|access-date=September 4, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250904170401/https://thenevadaindependent.com/article/democrat-alexis-hill-jumps-into-nevada-governor-race-unveils-revenue-raising-tax-plan|archive-date=September 4, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref>

Ford defeated Lombardo by about seven points.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-11-05 |title=Democrat Aaron Ford wins 2026 Nevada governor's race, defeating incumbent Gov. Joe Lombardo - CBS News |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/2026-midterm-elections-nevada-governors-race-results-aaron-ford-joe-lombardo/ |access-date=2026-11-14 |website=www.cbsnews.com |language=en-US}}</ref> Lombardo is the second consecutive governor of Nevada to lose re-election after [[Steve Sisolak]] in 2022. Ford became Nevada's first African American governor and the first Black person elected governor of a U.S. state west of the Mississippi River. Lombardo was one of two Republican governors to lose re-election in 2026, the other one being [[Greg Abbott]] in [[2026 Texas gubernatorial election|Texas]].
