Governor [[Michelle Lujan Grisham]], a Democrat, was re-elected in [[2022 New Mexico gubernatorial election|2022]] with 52.0% of the vote. She will be term-limited by the [[Constitution of New Mexico|New Mexico Constitution]] in 2026 and cannot seek re-election to a third consecutive term.

Former [[United States Secretary of the Interior|U.S. Secretary of the Interior]] and U.S. Representative [[Deb Haaland]] defeated [[Bernalillo County, New Mexico|Bernalillo County]] District Attorney Sam Bregman to win the Democratic nomination on June 2.<ref name="Haaland">{{cite news |last1=Lee |first1=Morgan |last2=Bryan |first2=Susan Montoya |title=Deb Haaland made history as Interior secretary. Now she's running for governor of New Mexico |url=https://apnews.com/article/deb-haaland-new-mexico-gubernatorial-campaign-284549dfb209b0007d0f9e9e550fb68d |access-date=January 28, 2025 |work=[[Associated Press]] |date=January 28, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250128052958/https://apnews.com/article/deb-haaland-new-mexico-gubernatorial-campaign-284549dfb209b0007d0f9e9e550fb68d |archive-date=January 28, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Bregman">{{cite news |last1=Rodriguez |first1=Vince |title=Sam Bregman announces candidacy for Governor in 2026 election |url=https://www.koat.com/article/sam-bregman-governor-candidate-2026-election/64435375 |access-date=April 10, 2025 |work=[[KOAT-TV]] |date=April 10, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250410203655/https://www.koat.com/article/sam-bregman-governor-candidate-2026-election/64435375 |archive-date=April 10, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

[[Rio Rancho, New Mexico|Rio Rancho]] mayor [[Gregg Hull]]<ref name="HullNM">{{cite news |last1=Hendircks |first1=Kevin |title=Rio Rancho mayor will join race for GOP nomination for governor |url=https://nmpoliticalreport.com/2025/04/15/rio-rancho-mayor-will-join-race-for-gop-nomination-for-governor/ |access-date=April 15, 2025 |work=[[New Mexico Political Report]] |date=April 15, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250416020811/https://nmpoliticalreport.com/2025/04/15/rio-rancho-mayor-will-join-race-for-gop-nomination-for-governor/ |archive-date=April 16, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> won the Republican nomination defeating former secretary of the New Mexico Human Services Department Duke Rodriguez<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bowling |first=Joshua |date=2025-12-15 |title=Duke Rodriguez formally announces Republican bid for governor |url=https://sourcenm.com/2025/12/15/duke-rodriguez-formally-announces-republican-bid-for-governor/ |access-date=2026-03-22 |website=Source New Mexico |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260302170943/https://sourcenm.com/2025/12/15/duke-rodriguez-formally-announces-republican-bid-for-governor/ |archive-date=March 2, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> and businessman Doug Turner.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Prokop |first=Danielle |date=2026-01-23 |title=New Mexico Election 2026: trail notes |url=https://sourcenm.com/2026/01/23/new-mexico-election-2026-trail-notes-3/ |access-date=2026-03-22 |website=Source New Mexico |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260310143707/https://sourcenm.com/2026/01/23/new-mexico-election-2026-trail-notes-3/ |archive-date=March 10, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Haaland defeated Hull by just over 14 points, becoming the first female Native American governor in American history.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Nowell |first=Cecilia |date=2026-11-04 |title=Deb Haaland wins in New Mexico and will become first female Native American governor |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/03/deb-haaland-new-mexico-governor |access-date=2026-11-14 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

