Governor [[Mike DeWine]], a Republican, was re-elected in [[2022 Ohio gubernatorial election|2022]] with 62.4% of the vote. He was term-limited by the [[Constitution of Ohio|Ohio Constitution]] in 2026 and could not seek re-election to a third consecutive term.

On the [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] side, [[Biotechnology|biotech]] entrepreneur and former candidate for the [[2024 Republican Party presidential primaries|Republican Party nomination]] in the 2024 presidential election [[Vivek Ramaswamy]] announced a campaign, which won the support of President Trump and Ohioan Vice President Vance.<ref name="Ramaswamy">{{Cite web |date=February 24, 2025 |title=Millionaire Vivek Ramaswamy set to join the Ohio governor's race |url=https://apnews.com/article/election-2026-ohio-governor-vivek-ramaswamy-799f0c8bdb38c43cd1c2846411867711 |access-date=February 24, 2025 |website=AP News |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250225014036/https://apnews.com/article/election-2026-ohio-governor-vivek-ramaswamy-799f0c8bdb38c43cd1c2846411867711 |archive-date=February 25, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Henninger |first=Taylor |date=2025-10-16 |title=Vivek Ramaswamy to make campaign stop in Ashland on Friday |url=https://www.ashlandsource.com/2025/10/16/vivek-ramaswamy-to-make-campaign-stop-in-ashland-on-friday/ |access-date=2025-11-27 |website=Ashland Source - Ashland County Ohio News & Info |language=en-US}}</ref> [[Ohio Attorney General]] [[Dave Yost]], who announced his candidacy for governor in January 2025, withdrew from the race and endorsed Ramaswamy in May 2025.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jordan |first1=Felicia |title='I am simply not that important': AG Dave Yost suspends his campaign to be Ohio's governor |url=https://www.wcpo.com/news/state/state-ohio/ag-dave-yost-suspends-his-campaign-to-be-ohios-governor |access-date=May 16, 2025 |work=[[WCPO-TV]] |date=May 16, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250516184122/https://www.wcpo.com/news/state/state-ohio/ag-dave-yost-suspends-his-campaign-to-be-ohios-governor |archive-date=May 16, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Ramaswamy defeated automotive entrepreneur Casey Putsch in the Republican primary on May 5, 2026.

Former [[Ohio Department of Health]] Director [[Amy Acton|Dr. Amy Acton]] is the Democratic nominee, as no other candidate filed by the February 4, 2026 deadline.<ref name="ActonOH">{{Cite web|url=https://www.axios.com/local/columbus/2025/01/07/amy-acton-ohio-governor-run-campaign|title=Amy Acton, former state health director, to campaign for Ohio governor|first=Tyler|last=Buchanan|date=January 7, 2025|website=Axios|access-date=January 7, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250107215632/https://www.axios.com/local/columbus/2025/01/07/amy-acton-ohio-governor-run-campaign|archive-date=January 7, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Press Releases |url=https://www.ohiosos.gov/office/media-center/categories/press-releases |access-date=2026-03-22 |website=Ohio Secretary of State |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260320113455/https://www.ohiosos.gov/office/media-center/categories/press-releases |archive-date=March 20, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

After a campaign described as "bitter" by the [[BBC]], Amy Acton won the election by an 8% margin.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-11-04 |title=Amy Acton wins Ohio governor race after Ramaswamy's attack ad marred bitter campaign |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cmx2dlz8574jo |access-date=2026-11-14 |website=www.bbc.com |language=en-GB}}</ref> This is the first time Democrats have won a gubernatorial election in Ohio since [[2006 Ohio gubernatorial election|2006]].
