[[Governor of Oklahoma|Governor]] [[Kevin Stitt]], a Republican, was re-elected in [[2022 Oklahoma gubernatorial election|2022]] with 55.4% of the vote. He will be term-limited by the [[Constitution of Oklahoma|Oklahoma Constitution]] in 2026 and cannot seek re-election to a third term.

[[Oklahoma Attorney General|Attorney General]] [[Gentner Drummond]],<ref name="DrummondOK">{{cite news |last1=Evans |first1=Murray |title=AG Gentner Drummond announces bid for Oklahoma governor in 2026 election |url=https://www.oklahoman.com/story/news/politics/state/2025/01/13/oklahoma-elections-gentner-drummond-campaign-governor-2026/77603880007/ |access-date=January 13, 2025 |work=[[The Oklahoman]] |date=January 13, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250113171135/https://www.oklahoman.com/story/news/politics/state/2025/01/13/oklahoma-elections-gentner-drummond-campaign-governor-2026/77603880007/ |archive-date=January 13, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> former Oklahoma Secretary of Budget [[Mike Mazzei]],<ref name="Mazzei">{{cite news |last1=Media |first1=Griffin |title=Oklahoma Governor race: Former State Sen. Mike Mazzei announces candidacy |url=https://www.newson6.com/story/67ea7ca61e03566cb076c088/oklahoma-governor-race-mike-mazzei |access-date=March 31, 2025 |work=[[KOTV-DT]] |date=March 31, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250331130124/http://www.newson6.com/story/67ea7ca61e03566cb076c088/oklahoma-governor-race-mike-mazzei |archive-date=March 31, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> former Speaker of the [[Oklahoma House of Representatives]] [[Charles McCall]],<ref name="McCall">{{cite news |last1=Media |first1=Griffin |title=Oklahoma Governor race: Charles McCall files for candidacy |url=https://www.news9.com/story/67b48d06a128e54ee89ada96/oklahoma-governor-race-charles-mccall-files-for-candidacy |access-date=February 18, 2025 |work=[[KWTV-DT]] |date=February 18, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250218135713/https://www.news9.com/story/67b48d06a128e54ee89ada96/oklahoma-governor-race-charles-mccall-files-for-candidacy |archive-date=February 18, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>  former [[Oklahoma Secretary of Public Safety]] [[Chip Keating]],<ref name="Keating">{{cite web |last1=Metzer |first1=Steve |title=Chip Keating announces run for governor |url=https://tulsaworld.com/news/state-regional/government-politics/article_f51a889e-1eec-4ddb-bd98-f52845f8c50b.html |access-date=October 2, 2025 |work=[[Tulsa World]] |date=October 1, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251002010622/https://tulsaworld.com/news/state-regional/government-politics/article_f51a889e-1eec-4ddb-bd98-f52845f8c50b.html |archive-date=October 2, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> who is the son of former governor [[Frank Keating]], and former [[Oklahoma Senate|state senator]] [[Jake A. Merrick]]<ref name="Merrick">{{cite news |last1=Ramos |first1=Lionel |title=Former lawmaker Jake Merrick joins race for Oklahoma Governor |url=https://www.kosu.org/politics/2025-05-01/former-lawmaker-jake-merrick-joins-race-for-oklahoma-governor |access-date=May 1, 2025 |work=[[KOSU]] |date=May 1, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506164227/https://www.kosu.org/politics/2025-05-01/former-lawmaker-jake-merrick-joins-race-for-oklahoma-governor |archive-date=May 6, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> all ran for the Republican nomination. Drummond and Mazzei advanced to a runoff, which took place on August 25. Mazzei narrowly defeated Drummond with 50.3% of the vote to become the Republican nominee.

[[Oklahoma House of Representatives|State representative]] [[Cyndi Munson]]<ref name="MunsonOK">{{cite news |last1=Media |first1=Griffin |title=Oklahoma House Rep. Cyndi Munson announces run for governor |url=https://www.newson6.com/story/67fe3542ef0ad866d416aaad/oklahoma-house-rep-cyndi-munson-announces-run-for-governor |access-date=April 15, 2025 |work=[[KOTV-DT]] |date=April 15, 2025 |language=en}}</ref> defeated securities trader Arya Azma<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hickey |first=Olivia |date=2025-11-24 |title=Gov. Kevin Stitt weighs in on crowded gubernatorial race, says he won't back AG Drummond |url=https://www.koco.com/article/kevin-stitt-governors-gubernatorial-race-ag-gentner-drummond/69533056 |access-date=2026-03-25 |website=KOCO |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251213001506/https://www.koco.com/article/kevin-stitt-governors-gubernatorial-race-ag-gentner-drummond/69533056 |archive-date=December 13, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> for the Democratic nomination.

Mazzei defeated Munson by six points. This was the best performance for a Democrat in a gubernatorial election in Oklahoma since [[2006 Oklahoma gubernatorial election|2006]], which was the last time a Democrat won, and the closest election since [[2002 Oklahoma gubernatorial election|2002]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hoberock |first=Barbara |date=2026-11-04 |title=Mike Mazzei, with Trump's backing, continues GOP dominance in Oklahoma governor win • Oklahoma Voice |url=https://oklahomavoice.com/2026/11/03/mike-mazzei-with-trumps-backing-continues-gop-dominance-in-oklahoma-governor-win/ |access-date=2026-11-14 |website=Oklahoma Voice |language=en-US}}</ref> 
