{{Main|2026 Oregon gubernatorial election}}

Governor [[Tina Kotek]], a Democrat, was elected in [[2022 Oregon gubernatorial election|2022]] with 47% of the vote. She is running for re-election to a second term.<ref name="Kotek">{{cite news |last1=Dole |first1=Bryce |title=Oregon Gov. Tina Kotek announces reelection bid |url=https://www.opb.org/article/2025/12/04/oregon-governor-tina-kotek-announces-reelection-bid/ |access-date=December 4, 2025 |work=[[Oregon Public Broadcasting]] |date=December 4, 2025}}</ref>

On the Republican side, former minority leader of the [[Oregon House of Representatives]] and [[2022 Oregon gubernatorial election|2022]] nominee for governor [[Christine Drazan]] defeated a field that included former professional basketball player and [[2010 Oregon gubernatorial election|2010]] nominee [[Chris Dudley]], [[Oregon House of Representatives|state representative]] [[Ed Diehl]], [[Marion County, Oregon|Marion County]] commissioner Danielle Bethell, [[Georgism|geonomics]] researcher Kyle Duyck, and candidate for [[Oregon Commissioner of Labor]] in 2022 Robert Neuman.<ref name="Drazan">{{Cite web |last=Fuentes |first=Carlos |date=2025-10-27 |title=Republican Christine Drazan will run for governor in 2026 |url=https://www.oregonlive.com/politics/2025/10/republican-christine-drazan-will-run-for-governor-in-2026.html |access-date=2025-10-27 |website=[[The Oregonian]] |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251027172305/https://www.oregonlive.com/politics/2025/10/republican-christine-drazan-will-run-for-governor-in-2026.html |archive-date=October 27, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="DudleyOR">{{Cite web |last=Fuentes |first=Carlos |date=2026-01-26 |title=Former Blazer Chris Dudley will run for Oregon governor, setting up heated Republican primary |url=https://www.oregonlive.com/politics/2026/01/former-blazer-chris-dudley-will-run-for-oregon-governor-setting-up-heated-republican-primary.html |access-date=2026-01-26 |website=oregonlive |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260126193725/https://www.oregonlive.com/politics/2026/01/former-blazer-chris-dudley-will-run-for-oregon-governor-setting-up-heated-republican-primary.html |archive-date=January 26, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="DiehlOR">{{Cite web |last=Fuentes |first=Carlos |date=2025-01-20 |title=Oregon Republican who led anti-tax referendum effort will run for governor |url=https://www.oregonlive.com/politics/2026/01/oregon-republican-who-led-anti-tax-referendum-effort-will-run-for-governor.html |access-date=2026-01-20 |website=[[The Oregonian]] |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260122065602/https://www.oregonlive.com/politics/2026/01/oregon-republican-who-led-anti-tax-referendum-effort-will-run-for-governor.html |archive-date=January 22, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=Bethell>{{Cite web |last=Moore |first=Madeleine |date=April 27, 2025 |title=Danielle Bethell, former Keizer chamber official, announces run for governor |url=https://www.keizertimes.com/2025/04/27/danielle-bethell-former-keizer-chamber-official-announces-run-for-governor/ |access-date=May 26, 2025 |website=Keizertimes |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250607163123/https://www.keizertimes.com/2025/04/27/danielle-bethell-former-keizer-chamber-official-announces-run-for-governor/ |archive-date=June 7, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Kotek won re-election by approximately 10 points, based on unofficial results. While Democrats have won every gubernatorial election in Oregon since [[1982 Oregon gubernatorial election|1982]], only one of these victories, in [[1998 Oregon gubernatorial election|1998]], has been by a margin greater than 10 points.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mason|first=Anastasia|title=Blue wave lifted Gov. Tina Kotek, but her margins tell a deeper story|url=https://www.statesmanjournal.com/story/news/politics/elections/2026/11/10/oregon-gov-tina-kotek-results-by-county/92700080007/|access-date=November 11, 2026|website=Statesman Journal|language=en-US}}</ref> Kotek became the first Oregon gubernatorial candidate to receive over a million votes.
