Governor [[Josh Shapiro]], a Democrat, was elected in [[2022 Pennsylvania gubernatorial election|2022]] with 56.5% of the vote. He ran for reelection to a second term and was the Democratic nominee.<ref name="Shapiro">{{cite news |last1=Ullery |first1=Chris |title=Gov. Josh Shapiro says he's officially running for reelection |url=https://www.phillyburbs.com/story/news/politics/2026/01/08/pa-governor-who-is-josh-shapiro-is-shapiro-running-for-reelection-president-top-democratic-candidate/88072092007/ |access-date=January 8, 2026 |work=[[Bucks County Courier Times]] |date=January 8, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260211092105/https://www.phillyburbs.com/story/news/politics/2026/01/08/pa-governor-who-is-josh-shapiro-is-shapiro-running-for-reelection-president-top-democratic-candidate/88072092007/ |archive-date=February 11, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> The Republican nominee was [[Treasurer of Pennsylvania|Pennsylvania Treasurer]] [[Stacy Garrity]].<ref name="Garrity">{{Cite news |last=Glueck |first=Katie |date=August 18, 2025 |title=Republican Stacy Garrity Announces Bid to Challenge Josh Shapiro in Pennsylvania |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/08/18/us/politics/republican-stacy-garrity-josh-shapiro-pennsylvania.html |access-date=August 19, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250819071234/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/08/18/us/politics/republican-stacy-garrity-josh-shapiro-pennsylvania.html |archive-date=August 19, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Shapiro comfortably defeated Garrity by more than 20 points.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Couloumbis |first=Angela |last2=White |first2=Jaxon |date=2026-11-03 |title=Josh Shapiro wins second term as Pennsylvania governor |url=https://www.spotlightpa.org/news/2026/11/election-results-pennsylvania-governor-josh-shapiro-stacy-garrity-elections/ |access-date=2026-11-14 |website=Spotlight PA |language=en-us}}</ref>{{clear}}
