{{Main|2026 South Carolina gubernatorial election}}

Governor [[Henry McMaster]], a Republican, was re-elected in [[2022 South Carolina gubernatorial election|2022]] with 58.1% of the vote. He is term-limited by the [[Constitution of South Carolina|South Carolina Constitution]] in 2026 and cannot seek re-election to a third consecutive full term.

Five Republicans contested the election; state senator [[Josh Kimbrell]],<ref name="Kimbrell">{{cite news |last1=Moore |first1=Stephanie |title=Sen. Josh Kimbrell announces run for SC governor |url=https://www.wyff4.com/article/josh-kimbrell-south-carolina-governor-run/65155657 |access-date=June 23, 2025 |work=[[WYFF]] |date=June 23, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250624121651/https://www.wyff4.com/article/josh-kimbrell-south-carolina-governor-run/65155657 |archive-date=June 24, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> attorney general [[Alan Wilson (politician)|Alan Wilson]],<ref name="Wilson">{{cite news |last1=Reynolds |first1=Nick |title=Attorney General Alan Wilson officially enters governor's race, kicking off battle of 2026 |url=https://www.postandcourier.com/politics/alan-wilson-announces-governor-south-carolina-republican/article_aa3496b4-e9d5-4a79-9421-94970ec67081.html |access-date=June 23, 2025 |work=[[The Post and Courier]] |date=June 23, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250624003941/https://www.postandcourier.com/politics/alan-wilson-announces-governor-south-carolina-republican/article_aa3496b4-e9d5-4a79-9421-94970ec67081.html |archive-date=June 24, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> lieutenant governor [[Pamela Evette]],<ref name="Evette">{{cite news |title=Lt. Governor Pamela Evette announces run for S.C. governor |url=https://www.abccolumbia.com/2025/07/14/lt-governor-pamela-evette-announces-run-for-s-c-governor/ |access-date=June 14, 2025 |work=ABC Columbia |date=July 14, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250714223159/https://www.abccolumbia.com/2025/07/14/lt-governor-pamela-evette-announces-run-for-s-c-governor/ |archive-date=July 14, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> and U.S. representatives [[Ralph Norman]]<ref name="NormanSC">{{cite news |last1=Kinnard |first1=Meg |title=Rep. Ralph Norman, among House's most conservative, set to enter South Carolina governor's race |url=https://apnews.com/article/ralph-norman-election-2026-governor-south-carolina-a3175ade72b18813d47c9bdf6f4e568b |access-date=July 25, 2025 |work=[[Associated Press]] |date=July 25, 2025 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250725110134/https://apnews.com/article/ralph-norman-election-2026-governor-south-carolina-a3175ade72b18813d47c9bdf6f4e568b |archive-date=July 25, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> and [[Nancy Mace]].<ref name="Mace">{{cite news |last1=Holdman |first1=Jessica |title=Rep. Nancy Mace officially enters SC governor's race |url=https://scdailygazette.com/2025/08/04/rep-nancy-mace-officially-enters-sc-governors-race/ |access-date=August 4, 2025 |work=South Carolina Daily Gazette |date=August 4, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250804121108/https://scdailygazette.com/2025/08/04/rep-nancy-mace-officially-enters-sc-governors-race/ |archive-date=August 4, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Evette and Wilson advanced to a runoff, which took place on June 23. Wilson won the runoff and became the Republican nominee.

On the Democratic side, [[South Dakota Democratic Party|state representative]] [[Jermaine Johnson (politician)|Jermaine Johnson]]<ref name="JohnsonSC">{{cite web |last1=Carpentier |first1=Bella |title=Democrat Jermaine Johnson formally joins 2026 race for governor of South Carolina |url=https://www.greenvilleonline.com/story/news/politics/2025/10/28/jermaine-johnson-announces-run-sc-governor-campaign/86945842007/ |access-date=October 28, 2025 |work=[[Greenville News]] |date=October 28, 2025}}</ref> was the nominee. Wilson defeated Johnson by four points, the closest South Carolina gubernatorial election since [[1994 South Carolina gubernatorial election|1994]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lomis |first=Connor |last2=Johncox |first2=Cassidy |date=2026-11-04 |title=Republican Alan Wilson wins South Carolina’s 2026 governor race, AP projects |url=https://www.wbtv.com/2026/11/04/republican-alan-wilson-wins-south-carolinas-2026-governor-race-ap-projects/ |access-date=2026-11-14 |website=WBTV |language=en}}</ref>
